  <h1>AI Question Paper Generator & Solution Engine</h1>
  <p><strong>Comprehensive System Architecture, Code Guide & Output Paste Sections</strong></p>
  <p><em>Generated Date: October 2026 | Format: Microsoft Word Document (.doc)</em></p>

  <hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #cbd5e1; margin: 20px 0;">

  <!-- Section 1 -->
  <h2>1. Project Overview</h2>
  <p>The <strong>AI Question Paper Generator</strong> is a web application designed to generate formatted academic examination papers, complete step-by-step solution keys, and step-by-step marking rubrics. The system allows users to specify subject parameters, difficulty levels, target grade, sub-topic focus, and total marks, and outputs print-ready exam documents.</p>

  <!-- Section 2 -->
  <h2>2. Tools & Technologies Used</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Category</th>
        <th>Technology / Tool</th>
        <th>Purpose & Functionality</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Frontend Markup</strong></td>
        <td>HTML5</td>
        <td>Provides semantic structure for the input configuration form, preset selectors, paper sheet display, and action buttons.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Styling & Design</strong></td>
        <td>CSS3 (Custom Design System)</td>
        <td>Implements clean typography (Inter font), background wallpaper integration, card elevation shadows, and <code>@media print</code> print layout engine.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Application Logic</strong></td>
        <td>Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+)</td>
        <td>Manages user input handling, DOM event listeners, dual AI generation routing, and interactive view switching.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>AI Generation Engine</strong></td>
        <td>Google Gemini 1.5 Flash API</td>
        <td>Generates structured JSON question papers via direct REST integration (<code>generativelanguage.googleapis.com</code>).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Offline Synthesis Engine</strong></td>
        <td>Built-in JavaScript Engine</td>
        <td>Fallback generator that synthesizes MCQs, Short Answer, and Long Answer questions instantly when no API key is provided.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Math Typesetting</strong></td>
        <td>KaTeX Math Engine</td>
        <td>Renders LaTeX mathematical and physical equations (e.g., Gauss Law, integrals, matrices, vectors) on the paper sheet.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Print & Document Export</strong></td>
        <td>CSS Print Engine & Canvas</td>
        <td>Formats the document into a standard university/school printable exam sheet for saving as PDF or printing directly.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <!-- Section 3 -->
  <h2>3. Codebase Architecture & File Guide</h2>

  <h3>3.1 File Structure</h3>
  <div class="code-block">
gen_ai/
├── index.html        # Main HTML layout, input form, and paper container
├── style.css         # Styling, wallpaper background, print rules
├── app.js            # Controller script: API calls, paper synthesis, DOM rendering
└── Project_Report.doc # Comprehensive report & output paste template
  </div>

  <h3>3.2 Detailed Code Explanation</h3>

  <h4>A. `index.html` (Markup & Structure)</h4>
  <p>Contains the input configuration form (Subject, Grade, Topic, Difficulty, Total Marks, Gemini API Key) and the output container with view toggle buttons (<em>Question Paper</em> vs <em>Answer Key & Solution</em>) and action triggers (<em>Print / Save PDF</em> and <em>Copy Text</em>).</p>

  <h4>B. `style.css` (Visual Design & Print Layout)</h4>
  <p>Configures a crisp off-white wallpaper background, card elevation shadows, and high-contrast typography. It contains a dedicated <code>@media print</code> section that hides all navigation elements and formats the exam paper onto clean white pages with standard margins when printing or saving as PDF.</p>

  <h4>C. `app.js` (Core Generator & Rendering Engine)</h4>
  <p>Contains the core JavaScript class <code>App</code> that handles:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Form Processing & Presets:</strong> Reads input fields or loads predefined sample configurations (Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, History).</li>
    <li><strong>Dual Generation Dispatch:</strong> If a Gemini API key is entered, it sends a structured JSON prompt to Gemini 1.5 Flash. Otherwise, it invokes the built-in <code>generateSynthesizedPaper()</code> method.</li>
    <li><strong>Dynamic DOM Rendering:</strong> Builds the exam header (Institution, Exam Title, Subject Code, Time, Marks), instructions, and sections (Section A: MCQs, Section B: Short Answer, Section C: Long Answer).</li>
    <li><strong>KaTeX LaTeX Integration:</strong> Calls <code>renderMathInElement()</code> to compile LaTeX formulas on the rendered paper sheet.</li>
  </ul>

